 "▼ Dive in: <0>pⁿ chart</0>": "",
 "An agent run is a chain of steps. If each step succeeds with probability <0>p</0> and steps were independent, the whole run succeeds with <1>pⁿ</1>.": "",
 "Even {#}% per step gives only ≈ {#}% after {#} steps: long tasks need verification, retries and checkpoints, not just a better model.": "",
 "Independence is a simplification: real errors are correlated, and agents can recover from some mistakes, so pⁿ is a sketch, not a prediction.": "",
 "Common failure modes: wrong tool, bad arguments, hallucinated results, loops, goal drift, context overflow, over-trusting tool output.": "",
