 "▼ Dive in: <0>Trace tree</0>": "",
 "You cannot improve what you cannot measure: an <0>eval set</0> (tasks + checks) turns \"seems better\" into numbers.": "",
 "A <0>trace</0> records every model call and tool call as a tree of spans, so you can see <1>why</1> a run failed.": "",
 "Because agents are stochastic, run each task several times: <0>pass@k</0> (any of k tries) and <1>pass^k</1> (all k tries) tell very different stories.": "",
 "Prefer programmatic graders (tests pass, row exists) when possible; use an LLM judge for open-ended quality, and calibrate it against human labels.": "",
 "LLM judges tend to show biases (position, verbosity, self-preference); mitigations help but do not remove them.": "",
